# yadm safety guard for ~/.claude. THE DOTFILES REPO IS PUBLIC, so the test for anything here is
# "would I post this to the internet", not "is this useful to keep".
#
# DEFAULT-DENY, deliberately. Claude Code and work installers both write new state into this
# directory continuously — caches, session logs, paste buffers, config backups, telemetry, skill
# symlinks — and an ignore list would have to grow to match. It never keeps up, and the failure
# mode is publishing something private. So: ignore everything, then allow the handful of files I
# actually curate. Anything new is private until I say otherwise.
#
# Notable things this keeps out, all of which a bare `yadm add -A .claude` would otherwise sweep:
# paste-cache/ (arbitrary pasted content), history.jsonl, projects/**/ (transcripts + agent memory
# carrying employer architecture), backups/ and settings.json.bak.* (UNFILTERED copies of settings,
# so they bypass the clean filter), security/, sessions/, and work skill/tool symlinks.

# Ignore everything at this level.
/*

# Allow only these.
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/settings.json
!/AI-SDLC.md
!/workflows/
!/skills/

# Within skills/, allowlist my own. Work installers symlink theirs in here, so default-deny means
# a newly shipped work skill is ignored without me having to notice it appeared.
/skills/*
!/skills/execute-plan/
!/skills/git-pr-workflow/
!/skills/scope-refine/
!/skills/staff-sre/
!/skills/staff-swe/

# Belt for the two files that ARE tracked but get rewritten by a work installer: their unfiltered
# backup copies must never be tracked, since they would leak what the clean filter strips.
settings.json.bak.*
CLAUDE.md.bak.*
